mentary requirements to Window 1 or 2\",\n          \"AGENCY ACTION: Certifies/Verifies Certificate of Enrollment\",\n          \"FEES TO BE PAID: None\",\n          \"PROCESSING TIME: 5 minutes\",\n          \"PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Mr. Roy E. Tagarao/Administrative Officer |||, Ms. Analene Grace P. Pagas/Administrative Aid |||, Mr. Earl Warren D. Caterial/Administrative Aid |||, Ms. Janet C. Cahatol/Administrative Aid |||\",\n          \"STEP 5:\",\n          \"CLIENT STEPS: Proceed to the validation of enrollment Accounting\",\n          \"AGENCY ACTION: Validates (for paying students only)\",\n          \"FEES TO BE PAID:\",\n          \"COB, COE, COT, CAS: P225.00/unit, Misc. Fee: P2,482.50\",\n          \"CON: P450.00/unit, Misc Fee:P4,070.00, RLE:P20,281.62\",\n          \"MASTERS: P400.00/unit, Misc Fee: P2,570.00\",\n          \"DOCTORATE: P600.00/unit, Misc Fee: P2,370.00\",\n          \"LAW: P600.00/unit, Misc Fee: P3,020.00\",\n          \"PROCESSING TIME: 6 minutes\",\n          \"PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Window 7- Kristrine B. Leria/Administrative Aid |||, Window 8- Liza B. Lambo/Administrative Aid |||, Window 9- Arvil A. Batobato/Administrative Aid |||, Ms. Minnelli G. Tumulak/Administrative Officer |, Ms. Karen D. Achacoso/Administrative Officer |||, Ms. Eunice E. Meliston/Cashier |||\",\n          \"TOTAL PROCESSING TIME: 55 minutes\"\n        ],\n        \"contact\": null,\n        \"last_updated\": \"2026-03-30T15:02:51.755Z\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nInstructions:\n- Use only facts present in CONTEXT_JSON.\n- If missing, return the exact no-info sentence.\n- Keep answer concise and factual.","model_response":"User Query:\nWhat is the process for Online Enrollment?\n\nThe process for Online Enrollment of New & Transferee Students is as follows:\n\n1. **Visit the Enrollment Platform**: Go to [admissions.buksu.edu.ph](https://www.admissions.buksu.edu.ph) and log in to your account. The credentials uploaded will be evaluated by the College/Department Enrollment Officer. (Processing Time: 4 minutes)\n\n2. **Apply and Upload Documents**: Apply for the desired program, enroll, and upload the necessary documentary requirements. The subjects will be loaded, and the Certificate of Registration (COR) will be uploaded at the same platform. (Processing Time: 30 minutes)\n\n3. **Review COR**: Download and review the COR. The enrollment application will be approved by the Enrollment Officer. (Processing Time: 10 minutes)\n\n4. **Submit Original Documents**: Submit original copies of documentary requirements to Window 1 or 2 for certification and verification of the Certificate of Enrollment. (Processing Time: 5 minutes)\n\n5. **Validation of Enrollment**: Proceed to the validation of enrollment at Accounting for paying students only. Fees vary by program. (Processing Time: 6 minutes)\n\nTotal Processing Time: 55 minutes.\n\nSources: 69bfa5bc355a381b553ea9e6.","retrieval_mode":"exact_fallback","vector_db":"in-memory-cosine","embedding_model":"hash-embedding-v1","type_filters":["Service"],"fallback":{"sql":"SELECT * FROM items WHERE canonical_name = ? OR aliases LIKE ? LIMIT 5","params":["process online enrollment","%process online enrollment%"],"matches":[{"id":"69b81d756915f5fd64f7d74d","type":"Service","canonical_name":"EXEMPTION SLIP","aliases":"EXEMPTION SLIP; ES; Student Leadership & Development Unit (SLEDEVU)","location":"Student Leadership & Development Unit (SLEDEVU)","last_updated":"2026-03-30T15:08:47.946Z","source":"services","content":"Service: EXEMPTION SLIP. Description: The exemption slip serves as a crucial tool in the university’s administrative framework, aiming to efficiently manage and formalize the process of excusing students for valid reasons. Aligned with established policies and procedures, it provides a transparent and fair mechanism for temporary absences from classes, events, or requirements.\n\nOffice or Division: Student Leadership & Development Unit\nClassification: Simple\nType of Transaction: G2C-Government to Citizen\nWho may avail: All enrolled students of Bukidnon State University. Requirements: -Validated Student Identification Card; -Letter request (Attachment to the declared reason for exemption). Process Steps: WHERE TO SECURE:; University Press (Refer to process on Securing School Identification Card); STEP 1: SUBMIT REQUIREMENTS; CLIENT STEPS: Present Identification Card & Printed Letter request with attachment.; AGENCY ACTION: Verify documents presented; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 1 minute; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Aaron Rod O. Corpuz / Jarey Mae E. Baylosis (SLeDevU Staff); STEP 2: RECORD AND ISSUANCE; CLIENT STEPS: Sign the Logbook.; AGENCY ACTION: Issue Exemption Slip; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 1 minute; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Aaron Rod O. Corpuz / Jarey Mae E. Baylosis (SLeDevU Staff); STEP 3: PROVIDE FEEDBACK; CLIENT STEPS: Fill out the Customer Feedback Form /BOSES.; AGENCY ACTION: Receives and monitors filled-out Customer Feedback Form; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 1 minute; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Aaron Rod O. Corpuz / Jarey Mae E. Baylosis (SLeDevU Staff); TOTAL Fees: None; TOTAL Processing Time: 3 Minutes. Department: . Office: Student Leadership & Development Unit (SLEDEVU)"},{"id":"69bfa5bc355a381b553ea9e6","type":"Service","canonical_name":"Online Enrollment of New & Transferee Students","aliases":"Online Enrollment of New & Transferee Students; OEON&TS; Registrar","location":"Registrar","last_updated":"2026-03-30T15:02:51.755Z","source":"services","content":"Service: Online Enrollment of New & Transferee Students. Description: High School/Senior High School graduates and Transferees from other private or government HEIs can apply for enrollment using the Online Enrollment platform at admissions.buksu.edu.ph\n\nOffice or Division: University Registrar's Office\nClassification: Complex\nType of Transaction: G2C-Government to Citizen\nWho may avail: External Clients (BukSU Students). Requirements: High School G