ATU)\",\n      \"similarity\": 0.99,\n      \"rerank_score\": 0.99,\n      \"rerank_signals\": {\n        \"exactCanonical\": true,\n        \"exactAlias\": false,\n        \"phraseCanonical\": true,\n        \"phraseAlias\": false,\n        \"sameTypeBoost\": 0,\n        \"stalenessPenalty\": 0\n      },\n      \"structured\": {\n        \"id\": \"69bf9b03355a381b553ea9da\",\n        \"name\": \"Claiming of Examination Result\",\n        \"requirements\": [],\n        \"details\": \"This refers to the release of the examinee's admission test result.\\nOffice or Division: Admission and Testing  Unit (ATU)\\nClassification: Simple\\nType of transaction: G2C-Government to Citizen\\nWho may avail: BukSU-CAT, COL & GPAT Takers\",\n        \"process_steps\": [\n          \"WHERE TO SECURE:\",\n          \"Admission account at admissions.buksu.edu.ph\",\n          \"STEP 1:\",\n          \"CLIENT STEPS: Login to admissions.buksu.edu.ph\",\n          \"ACTION AGENCY: Upload to admissions system 15 working days after the last conduct of BukSU-CAT/COL/GPAT.\",\n          \"FEES TO BE PAID: None\",\n          \"PROCESSING TIME: 5 minutes\",\n          \"PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Angel Sweet S. Berdiguel (ATU Psychometrician)\"\n        ],\n        \"contact\": null,\n        \"last_updated\": \"2026-03-30T14:33:42.877Z\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nInstructions:\n- Use only facts present in CONTEXT_JSON.\n- If missing, return the exact no-info sentence.\n- Keep answer concise and factual.","model_response":"User Query:\nClaiming of Examination Result\n\nThe claiming of examination results refers to the release of the examinee's admission test result. It is managed by the Admission and Testing Unit (ATU). The process involves logging into the admissions account at admissions.buksu.edu.ph. The results are uploaded to the admissions system 15 working days after the last conduct of BukSU-CAT/COL/GPAT. There are no fees, and the processing time is approximately 5 minutes. The person responsible is Angel Sweet S. Berdiguel, the ATU Psychometrician. Sources: 69bf9b03355a381b553ea9da.","response_text":"User Query:\nClaiming of Examination Result\n\nThe claiming of examination results refers to the release of the examinee's admission test result. It is managed by the Admission and Testing Unit (ATU). The process involves logging into the admissions account at admissions.buksu.edu.ph. The results are uploaded to the admissions system 15 working days after the last conduct of BukSU-CAT/COL/GPAT. There are no fees, and the processing time is approximately 5 minutes. The person responsible is Angel Sweet S. Berdiguel, the ATU Psychometrician. Sources: 69bf9b03355a381b553ea9da.","model_response_language":"english","final_response_language":"english","translation_steps":{"query":{"text":"Claiming of Examination Result","sourceLanguage":"english","targetLanguage":"english","translated":false,"method":"none"},"response":{"text":"User Query:\nClaiming of Examination Result\n\nThe claiming of examination results refers to the release of the examinee's admission test result. It is managed by the Admission and Testing Unit (ATU). The process involves logging into the admissions account at admissions.buksu.edu.ph. The results are uploaded to the admissions system 15 working days after the last conduct of BukSU-CAT/COL/GPAT. There are no fees, and the processing time is approximately 5 minutes. The person responsible is Angel Sweet S. Berdiguel, the ATU Psychometrician. Sources: 69bf9b03355a381b553ea9da.","sourceLanguage":"english","targetLanguage":"english","translated":false,"method":"none"}},"retrieval_mode":"exact_fallback","vector_db":"in-memory-cosine","embedding_model":"hash-embedding-v1","type_filters":[],"fallback":{"sql":"SELECT * FROM items WHERE canonical_name = ? OR aliases LIKE ? LIMIT 5","params":["claiming examination result","%claiming examination result%"],"matches":[{"id":"69b81d756915f5fd64f7d74d","record_id":"69b81d756915f5fd64f7d74d","type":"Service","canonical_name":"EXEMPTION SLIP","aliases":"EXEMPTION SLIP; ES; Student Leadership & Development Unit (SLEDEVU)","location":"Student Leadership & Development Unit (SLEDEVU)","last_updated":"2026-03-30T15:08:47.946Z","last_indexed":"2026-04-05T04:18:46.862Z","deactivated":false,"source":"services","content":"Service: EXEMPTION SLIP. Description: The exemption slip serves as a crucial tool in the university’s administrative framework, aiming to efficiently manage and formalize the process of excusing students for valid reasons. Aligned with established policies and procedures, it provides a transparent and fair mechanism for temporary absences from classes, events, or requirements. Office or Division: Student Leadership & Development Unit Classification: Simple Type of Transaction: G2C-Government to Citizen Who may avail: All enrolled students of Bukidnon State University. Requirements: -Validated Student Identification Card; -Letter request (Attachment to the declared reason for exemption). Process Steps: WHERE TO SECURE:; University Press (Refer to process on Securing School Identification Card); STEP 1: SUBMIT REQUIREMENTS; CLIENT STEPS: Present Identification Card & Printed Letter request with attachment.; AGENCY ACTION: Verify documents presented; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 1 minute; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Aaron Rod O. Corpuz / Jarey Mae E. Baylosis (SLeDevU Staff); STEP 2: RECORD AND ISSUANCE; CLIENT STEPS: Sign the Logbook.; AGENCY ACTION: Issue Exemption Slip; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 1 minute; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Aaron Rod O. Corpuz / Jarey Mae E. Baylosis (SLeDevU Staff); STEP 3: PROVIDE FEEDBACK; CLIENT STEPS: Fill out the Customer Feedback Form /BOSES.; AGENCY ACTION: Receives and monitors filled-out Customer Feedback Form; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 1 minute; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Aaron Rod O. Corpuz / Jarey Mae E. Baylosis (SLeDevU Staff); TOTAL Fees: None; TOTAL Processing Time: 3 Minutes. Department: . Office: Student Leadership & Development Unit (SLEDEVU)"},{"id":"69bf9b03355a381b553ea9da","record_id":"69bf9b03355a381b553ea9da","type":"Service","canonical_name":"Claiming of Examination Result","aliases":"Claiming of Examination Result; COER; Admission and Testing Unit (ATU)","location":"Admission and Testing Unit (ATU)","last_updated":"2026-03-30T14:33:42.877Z","last_indexed":"2026-04-05T04:18:46.863Z","deactivated":false,"source":"services","content":"Service: Claiming of Examination Result. Description: This refers to the release of the examinee's admission test result. Office or Division: Admission and Testing Unit (ATU) Classification: Simple Type of transaction: G2C-Government to Citizen Who may avail: BukSU-CAT, COL & GPAT Takers. Requirements: . Process Steps: WHERE TO SECURE:; Admission account at admissions.buksu.edu.ph; STEP 1:; CLIENT STEPS: Login to admissions.buksu.edu.ph; ACTION AGENCY: Upload to admissions system 15 working days after the last conduct of BukSU-CAT/COL/GPAT.; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 5 minutes; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Angel Sweet S. Berdiguel (ATU Psychometrician). Department: . Office: Admission and Testing Unit (ATU)"}]}}
