 Arts, Sports and Student Services (OVPCASSS)","location":"Office of the Vice President for Culture, Arts, Sports and Student Services (OVPCASSS)","last_updated":"2026-04-05T12:06:34.790Z","source":"services","content":"Service: Validation & Activation of School ID (Identification Card). Description: Refers to the process of verifying the authenticity and legitimacy of a student's identification card and enrollment in the university. This is usually done every semester to ensure that only registered students can access campus facilities and services. Office or Division: Office of the Vice President for Culture, Arts, Sports and Student Services Classification: Simple Type of transaction: G2C-Government to Citizen Who may avail: All enrolled students of Bukidnon State University. Requirements: Validated Certificate of Registration; Student Identification Card. Process Steps: WHERE TO SECURE:; Download your COR at https://admissions.buksu.edu.ph/ and proceed to the Accounting Office for validation; University Press; STEP 1:; CLIENT STEPS: Present printed Certificate of Registration and Identification Card; AGENCY ACTION: 1.1 Verifies data on Certificate of Registration and Identification Card 1.2 OVPCASSS staff activates the identification card, affixes the validation sticker for the specific semester, and then returns the ID to the student; FEES TO BE PAID: None; TOTAL PROCESSING TIME: 1 minute and 30 seconds; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: TWYLA B. GARCES/VINCENT REY G. CAINILA (OVPCASSS Staff). Department: . Office: Office of the Vice President for Culture, Arts, Sports and Student Services (OVPCASSS)","similarity":1,"rerank_score":1,"rerank_signals":{"exactCanonical":true,"exactAlias":false,"phraseCanonical":true,"phraseAlias":false,"sameTypeBoost":0,"stalenessPenalty":0},"structured":{"id":"69bf640e355a381b553ea8db","name":"Validation & Activation of School ID (Identification Card)","requirements":["Validated Certificate of Registration","Student Identification Card"],"deta