raduates, Transferees and ALS Graduates. Requirements: -2X2 picture with white background; -Scanned copy of Documentary Requirement:; a. For Senior High School Graduates: Report Card/Certification as part of the graduating class signed by the Adviser/School Head; b. For Transferees: Scanned copy of Honorable Dismissal and Scanned copy of Transcript of Records; -For ALS Completer: Scanned copy of test result and Report Card for ALS indicating eligibility to enroll in Tertiary Education Institution. Process Steps: WHERE TO SECURE:; Photo studio/Camera/Smart phones; School previously attended; Alternative Learning System community learning centers: ALS facilitator; STEP 1:; CLIENT STEPS: Access admissions.buksu.edu.ph on a browser and click \"Register\" or \"Login\"; AGENCY ACTION: The admission in-charge coordinates with the Data Center to open the application link for BukSU-CAT; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 5 minutes; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Mark G. Ochavillo (Document Controller); STEP 2:; CLIENT STEPS: Register an active email address and create a password. Read the privacy and terms agreement to next steps; AGENCY ACTION: An Automated privacy and terms agreement will notify the client and request their consent for BukSU ATU to access their personal information. This ensures compliance with data and privacy laws and allows to provide academic and administrative services.; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 5 minutes; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Mark G. Ochavillo (Document Controller); STEP 3:; CLIENT STEPS: Access Gmail inbox to activate admission account; AGENCY ACTION: The ATU sends automated email of activation link to the client; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 2 minutes; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Mark G. Ochavillo (Document Controller); STEP 4:; CLIENT STEPS: Proceed to complete the online application by providing the required information and submission of documentary requirement.; AGENCY ACTION: The Admission website prompts the client to provide the necessary information and uploaded the required documents to complete the application process.; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 10 minutes; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Mark G. Ochavillo (Document Controller); STEP 5:; CLIENT STEPS: Proceed to select date and time of the admission test.; AGENCY ACTION: The admission in-charge manages and opens the examination schedules for applicants; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 5 minutes; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Mark G. Ochavillo (Document Controller); STEP 6:; CLIENT STEPS: Submit the accomplished online application for evaluation; AGENCY ACTION: The admission in-charge evaluates the applications. (Evaluation is done per testing schedule); FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 5 minutes; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Mark G. Ochavillo (Document Controller); TOTAL PROCESSING TIME: 32 minutes. Department: . Office: Admission and Testing Unit (ATU)"},{"id":"69bf9864355a381b553ea98f","record_id":"69bf9864355a381b553ea98f","type":"Service","canonical_name":"Conduct of Entrance Examination for Incoming College Students","role_title":"Admission and Testing Unit (ATU)","aliases":"Conduct of Entrance Examination for Incoming College Students; COEEFICS; Conduct of Entrance Examination for Incoming College Students service; Admission and Testing Unit (ATU); cnduct of entrance examination for incoming college students; conduct of etrance examination for incoming college students; conduct of entrance eamination for incoming college students; conduct of entrance examination for icoming college students; conduct of entrance examination for incoming cllege students; conduct of entrance examination for incoming college sudents; con; con of entrance examination for incoming college students; cond; cond of entrance examination for incoming college students; conduc; conduc of entrance examination for incoming college students; ent; conduct of ent examination for incoming college students; entr; conduct of entr examination for incoming college students; 