dule for Senior High School, ALS graduates and Transferees who have the intention to enroll in any undergraduate programs of the university. Office or Division: Admission and Testing Unit (ATU) Classification: Complex Type of Transaction: G2C- Government to Citizen Who may avail: High School Graduates, Transferees and ALS Graduates","requirements":"-2X2 picture with white background; -Scanned copy of Documentary Requirement:; a. For Senior High School Graduates: Report Card/Certification as part of the graduating class signed by the Adviser/School Head; b. For Transferees: Scanned copy of Honorable Dismissal and Scanned copy of Transcript of Records; -For ALS Completer: Scanned copy of test result and Report Card for ALS indicating eligibility to enroll in Tertiary Education Institution","process":"WHERE TO SECURE:; Photo studio/Camera/Smart phones; School previously attended; Alternative Learning System community learning centers: ALS facilitator; STEP 1:; CLIENT STEPS: Access admissions.buksu.edu.ph on a browser and click \"Register\" or \"Login\"; AGENCY ACTION: The admission in-charge coordinates with the Data Center to open the application link for BukSU-CAT; FEES TO BE PAID: None; PROCESSING TIME: 5 minutes; PERSON RESPONSIBLE: Mark G. Ochavillo (Document Controller); STEP 2:; CLIENT STEPS: Register an active email address and create a password. Read the privacy and terms agreement to next steps; AGENCY ACTION: An Automated privacy and terms agreement will notify the client and request their consent for BukSU ATU to access their personal information. This ensures compliance with data and privacy laws and allows to provide academic and administrative services.; STEP 3:; CLIENT STEPS: Access Gmail inbox to activate admission account; AGENCY ACTION: The ATU sends automated email of activation link to the client; PROCESSING TIME: 2 minutes; STEP 4:; CLIENT STEPS: Proceed to complete the online application by providing the required information and submission of doc