ocess it, and will send you a softcopy of your certificate through the email that you will be providing us through BUKSU-OSS.","category":null,"keywords":[],"alternativeQuestions":[],"stakeholder":null,"stakeholders":[],"source":null,"status":"verified","effectiveDate":null,"expirationDate":null,"officeId":null,"officeName":null,"departmentId":null,"departmentName":null,"contact":null,"relatedFaqs":[],"resources":[],"downloadableResources":[],"verificationStatus":"verified","verified":true,"verifiedBy":null,"lastVerified":"2026-08-12T16:44:52.046Z","sourceOffice":null,"last_updated":"2026-08-12T16:44:52.282Z"}}],"chosen_match":{"id":"6a7ca304f97e224f634e5ef3","type":"FAQ","canonical_name":"How to get good moral certificate and other certifications? (e.g. certifications for PNP application, certifications of not enjoying scholarship)","is_active":true},"chosen_similarity_score":99,"chosen_confidence_score":100,"chosen_lexical_match":false,"model_response":"If you’re capable of going to the University Campus, you need to get the request form through the University Guards at the University Exit Gate and the form should be filled up before giving it back to the Staff/The University Guard. You also have to pay P50.00 for the certificate, and it will be paid to the cashier by the staff assigned/the university guards. The staff assigned/the University Guard will forward the receipt and the request form to the Office of the Student Services. The Staff will then process it, print it, and have it signed by the OSS Dean. Lastly, the Staff will bring your good moral certificate to you at the exit gate, and you just have to fill-up the Good Moral Certificate Logbook. If requesting online, you need to message our Facebook page, BUKSU-OSS for your request. The staff will then accommodate you by sending the BUKSU account details for you to deposit your payment to. Deposit your payment to the account provided. After depositing, you need to submit back a clear or scanned picture of your deposit slip. It would take 2-3 days to settle your payment between the accounting unit and the bank. The Office of the Student Services will then process it, and will send you a softcopy of your certificate through the email that you will be providing us through BUKSU-OSS.","response_text":"If you’re capable of going to the University Campus, you need to get the request form through the University Guards at the University Exit Gate and the form should be filled up before giving it back to the Staff/The University Guard. You also have to pay P50.00 for the certificate, and it will be paid to the cashier by the staff assigned/the university guards. The staff assigned/the University Guard will forward the receipt and the request form to the Office of the Student Services. The Staff will then process it, print it, and have it signed by the OSS Dean. Lastly, the Staff will bring your good moral certificate to you at the exit gate, and you just have to fill-up the Good Moral Certificate Logbook. If requesting online, you need to message our Facebook page, BUKSU-OSS for your request. The staff will then accommodate you by sending the BUKSU account details for you to deposit your payment to. Deposit your payment to the account provided. After depositing, you need to submit back a clear or scanned picture of your deposit slip. It would take 2-3 days to settle your payment between the accounting unit and the bank. The Office of the Student Services will then process it, and will send you a softcopy of your certificate through the email that you will be providing us through BUKSU-OSS.","response_type":"VERIFIED_ANSWER","verification_status":"verified","knowledge_source":"ALAGAD FAQ","final_response_language":"english","retrieval_category":"Description","retrieval_mode":"exact_fallback","vector_db":"chromadb","embedding_model":"hash-embedding-v1"}
